// Eager collection methods (prelude-redesign P1): `map`/`filter`/`sum` are list methods (the eager
// forms, returning a `List`/value directly, distinct from the lazy `xs.iter().map(...)` adapters),
// and `len()` is the length of any collection (the preferred name for what `count()` did). Each
// reuses the existing free-function/`count` implementation, so both backends agree by construction.
// expect: stdout "[2, 4, 6]"
// expect: stdout "[2, 4]"
// expect: stdout "6"
// expect: stdout "3"
// expect: stdout "3"
// expect: stdout "2"
// expect: stdout "5"
// expect: exit 0
xs = [1, 2, 3]

echo xs.map(fn(v) => v * 2)
echo xs.filter(fn(v) => v % 2 == 0) ~ [4]
echo xs.sum()
echo xs.len()
echo {"a": 1, "b": 2, "c": 3}.len()
echo [1, 2].to_set().len()
echo "hello".len()
